cation is deemed granted.\n","versionId":"riverbend-amendment-2-draft"},{"citation":"§ 2","id":"s2","parentId":null,"path":"2","span":{"end":10,"kind":"line","start":10},"text":"Section 2. Eligibility.","versionId":"riverbend-amendment-2-draft"},{"citation":"§ 2(a)","id":"s2.a","parentId":"s2","path":"2(a)","span":{"end":11,"kind":"line","start":11},"text":"(a) The Licensing Office shall grant a permit to an applicant who holds liability insurance and has passed a fire safety inspection.","versionId":"riverbend-amendment-2-draft"},{"citation":"§ 2(b)","id":"s2.b","parentId":"s2","path":"2(b)","span":{"end":12,"kind":"line","start":12},"text":"(b) The Licensing Office shall deny a permit to an applicant who does not meet subsection (a).","versionId":"riverbend-amendment-2-draft"},{"citation":"§ 2(c)","id":"s2.c","parentId":"s2","path":"2(c)","span":{"end":14,"kind":"line","start":13},"text":"(c) Subsection (b) does not apply to an insured applicant whose requested fire safety inspection has not yet been performed. The Licensing Office shall issue that applicant a provisional permit.\n","versionId":"riverbend-amendment-2-draft"},{"citation":"§ 3","id":"s3","parentId":null,"path":"3","span":{"end":15,"kind":"line","start":15},"text":"Section 3. Fees.","versionId":"riverbend-amendment-2-draft"},{"citation":"§ 3(a)","id":"s3.a","parentId":"s3","path":"3(a)","span":{"end":16,"kind":"line","start":16},"text":"(a) A permit holder shall pay a permit fee of 250 dollars to the Town.","versionId":"riverbend-amendment-2-draft"},{"citation":"§ 3(b)","id":"s3.b","parentId":"s3","path":"3(b)","span":{"end":18,"kind":"line","start":17},"text":"(b) A nonprofit organization is exempt from the fee in subsection (a).\n","versionId":"riverbend-amendment-2-draft"},{"citation":"§ 4","id":"s4","parentId":null,"path":"4","span":{"end":19,"kind":"line","start":19},"text":"Section 4. Appeals.","versionId":"riverbend-amendment-2-draft"},{"citation":"§ 4(a)","id":"s4.a","parentId":"s4","path":"4